WEBVTT

00:00:12.490 --> 00:00:18.640
Do you hear?  Hooves beating

00:00:25.430 --> 00:00:30.750
A carriage goes through the gentle hills

00:00:33.100 --> 00:00:38.030
Someone comes to pick me up

00:00:39.100 --> 00:00:45.980
And takes me

00:00:46.250 --> 00:00:49.950
To the avenue with white flowers

00:00:52.640 --> 00:00:58.070
To the home of wind

00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:02.450
He takes me

00:01:05.200 --> 00:01:08.900
I'm sure

00:01:38.710 --> 00:01:40.820
Anne did not confess.

00:01:40.820 --> 00:01:43.350
Wednesday morning dawned
as bright and fair

00:01:43.350 --> 00:01:47.310
as if expressly made to
order for the picnic.

00:01:48.830 --> 00:01:52.600
Matthew and Jerry Buote
had gone to buy hay,

00:01:52.600 --> 00:01:56.890
when Marilla took breakfast to Anne,
with a heavy heart.

00:02:08.530 --> 00:02:09.450
Marilla...

00:02:11.610 --> 00:02:13.610
I'm ready to confess.

00:02:13.610 --> 00:02:15.750
Ah! Finally.

00:02:20.470 --> 00:02:22.990
Let me hear what you have
to say then, Anne.

00:02:25.290 --> 00:02:28.350
I took the amethyst brooch.

00:02:30.220 --> 00:02:33.010
I took it just as you said.

00:02:33.010 --> 00:02:35.940
I didn't mean to take it when I went in.

00:03:31.820 --> 00:03:36.230
But it did look so beautiful,
when I pinned it on my breast

00:03:36.230 --> 00:03:38.950
that I was overcome by
an irresistible temptation.

00:03:43.340 --> 00:03:48.720
I imagined how perfectly thrilling it
would be to take it to Idlewild

00:03:48.720 --> 00:03:51.330
and play I was the
Lady Cordelia Fitzgerald.

00:03:51.740 --> 00:03:55.290
It would be so much easier to
imagine I was the Lady Cordelia

00:03:55.290 --> 00:03:59.030
if I had a real amethyst brooch on.

00:04:00.450 --> 00:04:04.270
Diana and I make necklaces
of roseberries,

00:04:04.280 --> 00:04:08.230
but what are roseberries
compared to amethysts?

00:04:09.160 --> 00:04:12.130
So I took the brooch.

00:04:14.590 --> 00:04:18.630
I thought I could put it back
before you came home.

00:04:19.330 --> 00:04:25.630
I went all the way around by the
road to lengthen out the time.

00:04:26.130 --> 00:04:30.050
When I was going over the bridge
across the Lake of Shining Waters

00:04:30.050 --> 00:04:33.320
I took the brooch off to
have another look at it.

00:04:46.150 --> 00:04:52.290
Oh, how it did shine in the sunlight!

00:05:09.210 --> 00:05:14.070
And then, when I was leaning over the
bridge, it just slipped through my fingers

00:05:14.070 --> 00:05:17.150
and went down--down--down,
all purply-sparkling.

00:05:18.380 --> 00:05:22.930
And sank forevermore beneath
the Lake of Shining Waters.

00:05:24.850 --> 00:05:27.580
And that's the best I can do at confessing.

00:05:30.940 --> 00:05:32.960
Anne, this is terrible.

00:05:32.960 --> 00:05:36.150
You are the very wickedest
girl I ever heard of.

00:05:36.370 --> 00:05:38.540
Yes, I suppose I am.

00:05:39.040 --> 00:05:42.160
And I know I'll have to be punished.

00:05:42.330 --> 00:05:47.010
It'll be your duty to punish me, Marilla.
Won't you please get it over right off?

00:05:47.780 --> 00:05:51.610
Because I'd like to go to the
picnic with nothing on my mind.

00:05:51.610 --> 00:05:56.290
Picnic, indeed! You'll go to no
picnic today, Anne Shirley.

00:05:56.290 --> 00:05:58.230
That shall be your punishment.

00:05:58.480 --> 00:06:02.000
And it isn't half severe enough
either for what you've done!

00:06:02.170 --> 00:06:04.210
Not go to the picnic!

00:06:05.040 --> 00:06:07.700
But you PROMISED me I might!

00:06:07.810 --> 00:06:12.530
Oh, Marilla, I must go to the picnic.
That was why I confessed.

00:06:13.070 --> 00:06:16.740
Punish me any way you like but that.

00:06:16.740 --> 00:06:20.540
Oh, Marilla, please,
let me go to the picnic.

00:06:21.820 --> 00:06:24.450
Think of the ice cream!

00:06:24.450 --> 00:06:27.520
For anything you know I may never have
a chance to taste ice cream again.

00:06:27.520 --> 00:06:29.460
You needn't plead, Anne.

00:06:29.460 --> 00:06:32.340
You are not going to the
picnic and that's final.

00:06:32.340 --> 00:06:34.570
No, not a word.

00:07:05.290 --> 00:07:08.010
I believe the child is crazy.

00:07:08.010 --> 00:07:11.710
No child in her senses
would behave as she does.

00:07:12.680 --> 00:07:15.710
If she isn't, she's utterly bad.

00:07:17.740 --> 00:07:20.730
I'm afraid Rachel was
right from the first.

00:07:27.190 --> 00:07:31.110
But I've put my hand to the
plow and I won't look back.

00:07:44.160 --> 00:07:47.170
That was a dismal morning.

00:07:47.990 --> 00:07:50.610
Marilla worked fiercely and
scrubbed the porch floor...

00:07:51.450 --> 00:07:55.570
and the dairy shelves when she
could find nothing else to do.

00:07:56.430 --> 00:07:59.320
Neither the shelves nor
the porch needed it,

00:07:59.320 --> 00:08:01.930
but Marilla did.

00:09:07.450 --> 00:09:09.160
It looks delicious.

00:09:09.160 --> 00:09:11.060
Diana, could you get me a basket?

00:09:11.060 --> 00:09:12.980
Well? Does it look good on me?

00:09:13.650 --> 00:09:17.630
Yes, it does.
Or else I wouldn't have made it for you.

00:09:18.200 --> 00:09:19.010
You're right.

00:09:20.040 --> 00:09:21.100
Hurry, hurry, hurry!

00:09:21.100 --> 00:09:22.750
It's almost finished.

00:09:25.010 --> 00:09:28.050
Anne's never had ice cream before.

00:09:28.530 --> 00:09:31.150
So she's really looking
forward to today's picnic.

00:09:31.150 --> 00:09:32.070
Really?

00:09:57.170 --> 00:09:59.620
Come down to your dinner, Anne.

00:10:16.670 --> 00:10:18.580
I don't want any dinner.

00:10:21.820 --> 00:10:23.600
I couldn't eat anything.

00:10:23.760 --> 00:10:25.760
My heart is broken.

00:10:26.110 --> 00:10:31.900
You'll feel remorse of conscience
someday, I expect, for breaking it, Marilla.

00:10:34.210 --> 00:10:36.850
But I forgive you.

00:10:36.860 --> 00:10:40.470
Remember when the time
comes that I forgive you.

00:10:41.490 --> 00:10:45.190
But please don't ask me to eat anything.

00:10:45.440 --> 00:10:48.170
Especially boiled pork and greens.

00:10:48.170 --> 00:10:53.990
Boiled pork and greens are so
unromantic when one is in affliction.

00:11:14.000 --> 00:11:15.680
Ice cream...

00:11:22.310 --> 00:11:28.630
Well now, she shouldn't have taken the
brooch, or told stories about it.

00:11:28.640 --> 00:11:33.790
But she's such an interesting little thing.

00:11:33.790 --> 00:11:37.890
Don't you think it's pretty rough not to let
her go to the picnic when she's so set on it?

00:11:37.890 --> 00:11:40.910
Matthew Cuthbert, I'm amazed at you.

00:11:41.600 --> 00:11:45.370
I think I've let her off entirely too easy.

00:11:46.380 --> 00:11:50.760
And she doesn't appear to realize
how wicked she's been at all.

00:11:51.330 --> 00:11:53.770
That's what worries me most.

00:11:54.160 --> 00:11:59.310
If she'd really felt sorry
it wouldn't be so bad.

00:12:01.690 --> 00:12:04.670
And you don't seem to realize it, neither.

00:12:04.870 --> 00:12:07.610
You're making excuses for her all the time.

00:12:08.860 --> 00:12:11.700
Well now, she's...

00:12:16.390 --> 00:12:20.240
She's such a little thing.

00:12:20.400 --> 00:12:25.720
And there should be allowances made.
You know she's never had any bringing up.

00:12:25.900 --> 00:12:27.990
Well, she's having it now.

00:14:11.620 --> 00:14:14.130
Right, I almost forgot!

00:14:14.750 --> 00:14:17.290
I need to go mend my shawl.

00:14:52.000 --> 00:14:55.000
Dear heart, what does this mean?

00:14:55.580 --> 00:15:00.890
Here's my brooch safe and sound that I
thought was at the bottom of Barry's pond.

00:15:05.730 --> 00:15:10.670
Whatever did that girl mean by
saying she took it and lost it?

00:15:15.090 --> 00:15:18.300
I believe Green Gables is bewitched.

00:15:20.390 --> 00:15:22.400
I remember now.

00:15:22.400 --> 00:15:26.530
When I took off my shawl Monday afternoon,
I laid it on the bureau for a minute.

00:15:35.390 --> 00:15:38.040
Oh my, I have to hurry!

00:16:03.740 --> 00:16:07.260
Jerry Buote, prepare the carriage.

00:16:07.260 --> 00:16:08.980
It's an emergency.

00:16:29.660 --> 00:16:30.740
I'm coming in, Anne.

00:16:35.540 --> 00:16:36.420
Anne Shirley.

00:16:46.010 --> 00:16:49.750
I've just found my brooch
hanging to my black lace shawl.

00:16:49.750 --> 00:16:54.080
Now I want to know what that rigmarole
you told me this morning meant.

00:16:54.080 --> 00:17:01.130
Why, you said you'd keep me here
until I confessed, didn't you?

00:17:01.590 --> 00:17:04.360
So I decided to confess.

00:17:05.640 --> 00:17:08.470
Because I was bound to get to the picnic.

00:17:10.300 --> 00:17:14.880
I thought out a confession last
night after I went to bed

00:17:15.220 --> 00:17:17.550
and made it as interesting as I could.

00:17:18.080 --> 00:17:21.760
And I said it over and over so that
I wouldn't forget it.

00:17:22.100 --> 00:17:27.500
But you wouldn't let me go
to the picnic after all,

00:17:28.270 --> 00:17:31.380
so all my trouble was wasted.

00:17:45.320 --> 00:17:46.670
Sorry, sorry!

00:17:47.000 --> 00:17:51.700
Anne, you do beat all!
But I was wrong. I see that now.

00:17:51.700 --> 00:17:54.750
I shouldn't have doubted your word...

00:17:55.680 --> 00:17:58.290
when I'd never known you to tell a story.

00:18:00.240 --> 00:18:05.380
Of course, it wasn't right for you to
confess to a thing you hadn't done.

00:18:05.860 --> 00:18:07.650
It was very wrong to do so.

00:18:07.650 --> 00:18:10.890
But I drove you to it.

00:18:10.890 --> 00:18:16.990
So if you'll forgive me,
Anne, I'll forgive you.

00:18:19.150 --> 00:18:21.490
And we'll start square again.

00:18:21.710 --> 00:18:24.210
And now get yourself ready for the picnic.

00:18:26.680 --> 00:18:28.450
Ice cream!

00:18:29.390 --> 00:18:32.130
But, Marilla, isn't it too late?

00:18:32.130 --> 00:18:36.300
No, it's only two o'clock.
An hour before it starts.

00:18:36.770 --> 00:18:40.070
Wash your face and comb your
hair and put on your gingham.

00:18:41.250 --> 00:18:44.960
I'll fill a basket for you. There's
plenty of stuff baked in the house.

00:18:44.960 --> 00:18:49.270
And Jerry Buote will drive you
down to the picnic ground.

00:18:49.270 --> 00:18:50.930
Oh, Marilla!

00:18:53.840 --> 00:19:00.300
Five minutes ago I was so miserable
I was wishing I'd never been born...

00:19:02.440 --> 00:19:05.470
and now I wouldn't change
places with an angel!

00:19:05.470 --> 00:19:08.140
Hurry up if you want your ice cream.

00:19:16.600 --> 00:19:18.070
Oh, so many!

00:19:19.020 --> 00:19:20.860
Those cherries are from
Snow Queen, aren't they?

00:19:21.220 --> 00:19:23.760
There are some freshly things inside.

00:19:24.130 --> 00:19:25.280
Here, you can go.

00:19:25.280 --> 00:19:26.770
Thank you, Marilla.

00:19:26.900 --> 00:19:27.950
I'm going!

00:19:28.160 --> 00:19:30.860
Be careful, don't hurt yourself!

00:19:36.040 --> 00:19:37.570
Jerry, hurry up.

00:19:37.900 --> 00:19:38.720
Yes.

00:19:38.720 --> 00:19:39.720
I'm going.

00:19:58.640 --> 00:20:01.940
Diana!

00:20:04.610 --> 00:20:05.420
Anne!

00:20:52.440 --> 00:20:55.380
Come on, the Ice cream is ready.

00:20:58.110 --> 00:21:00.010
Ice cream!

00:21:45.500 --> 00:21:50.190
Oh, Marilla, I've had a perfectly
scrumptious time.

00:21:50.190 --> 00:21:54.240
Scrumptious is a new word I learned today.

00:21:54.240 --> 00:21:58.200
I heard Mary Bell use it.
Isn't it very expressive?

00:21:59.050 --> 00:22:00.730
Everything was lovely.

00:22:01.030 --> 00:22:02.760
We had a splendid tea

00:22:02.760 --> 00:22:07.560
and then Mr. Harmon Andrews took us all
for a row on the Lake of Shining Waters.

00:22:07.560 --> 00:22:11.620
And Jane Andrews nearly fell overboard.

00:22:11.930 --> 00:22:14.520
She was leaning out to pick water lilies

00:22:14.520 --> 00:22:18.700
and if Mr. Andrews hadn't caught her
by her sash just in the nick of time

00:22:18.700 --> 00:22:21.520
she'd fallen in and probably been drowned.

00:22:21.930 --> 00:22:24.730
I wish it had been me.

00:22:25.660 --> 00:22:29.590
It would have been such a romantic
experience to have been nearly drowned.

00:22:32.120 --> 00:22:35.340
And we had the ice cream.

00:22:35.690 --> 00:22:42.720
Words fail me to describe that ice cream,
Marilla. I assure you it was sublime.

00:22:43.000 --> 00:22:47.350
I wonder if that's the right word to
use to describe something delicious.

00:22:58.570 --> 00:23:02.030
I'm willing to own up that I made a mistake.

00:23:02.190 --> 00:23:04.300
But I've learned a lesson.

00:23:04.300 --> 00:23:08.190
I have to laugh when I think
of Anne's confession,

00:23:08.190 --> 00:23:12.930
although I suppose I shouldn't
for it really was a falsehood.

00:23:13.380 --> 00:23:19.090
But it doesn't seem as bad as the
other would have been, somehow,

00:23:19.090 --> 00:23:22.300
and anyhow I'm responsible for it.

00:23:25.010 --> 00:23:28.200
That child is hard to
understand in some respects.

00:23:28.610 --> 00:23:32.210
But I believe she'll turn out all right yet.

00:23:34.910 --> 00:23:41.850
And there's one thing certain,
no house will ever be dull that she's in.

00:23:42.350 --> 00:23:44.160
Well now, you're right.

00:24:18.470 --> 00:24:22.110
Anne went to school with
Diana with excitement.

00:24:22.340 --> 00:24:25.650
Next episode of Anne of Green Gables:

00:24:25.650 --> 00:24:27.610
Anne Goes To School

00:24:27.610 --> 00:24:28.940
Please watch!
